<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joseph Gallieni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1849–1916</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joseph Gallieni was a French army officer and colonial administrator who commanded in the Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> region of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> in the 1880s and served in Tonkin. As governor-general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> from 1896 to 1905 he abolished the Merina monarchy in 1897, exiled Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranavalona-iii">Ranavalona III</a> and crushed resistance. Military governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1914, he helped win the Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marne">Marne</a> and was made a marshal after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joseph-gallieni.jpg" alt="Joseph Gallieni" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bain News Service, publisher · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gen._Gallieni_LCCN2014697689_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
